cask "skald" do
  version "@VERSION@"
  sha256 "@SHA256@"

  url "https://github.com/michaelrigart/skald/releases/download/#{version}/Skald-#{version}.zip"
  name "Skald"
  desc "Spelling and grammar checker for the menu bar"
  homepage "https://github.com/michaelrigart/skald"

  livecheck do
    url :url
    regex(/^(\d{8}-\d{4})$/i)
    strategy :github_latest
  end

  depends_on arch: :arm64
  depends_on macos: :golden_gate

  app "Skald.app", target: "/Applications/Skald.app"

  uninstall quit: "com.michaelrigart.skald"

  zap trash: [
    "~/Library/Application Support/com.michaelrigart.skald",
    "~/Library/Preferences/com.michaelrigart.skald.plist",
  ]

  caveats <<~EOS
    Skald is signed but not notarized, so macOS blocks its first launch.
    After the first install, open System Settings > Privacy & Security and
    choose "Open Anyway" for Skald. Upgrades should not need this again.

    Then allow Skald under Accessibility in System Settings > Privacy &
    Security. Upgrades should keep this permission; if macOS asks again,
    repeat it.

    Checks by the on-device model need Apple Intelligence turned on in
    System Settings.

    "brew uninstall --zap" keeps the Keychain item that holds your Claude API
    key (service com.michaelrigart.skald, account claude-api-key). The README
    says how to delete it.
  EOS
end
